 Up is the historical frequency of a strictly positive return; P10–P90 is the middle 80% of observed returns, not a forecast range. Fewer than 10 outcomes: no headline return estimate. Fewer than 20: thin sample; this threshold does not validate a forecast. Price returns use cached Bloomberg PX_LAST; dividend and corporate-action adjustments were not independently verified. The dashboard shows P10–P90 dispersion, calendar-block intervals and 2024–25 versus 2026 stability. QQQ benchmark prices through 2026-09-25; missing benchmark dates are not filled.</p><a style="color:#9dc0ff" href="http://DS-CAP-33:8080/wiki/_dashboards/attention-sentiment/score-returns.html">Explore score bands, dispersion and historical periods →</a></section><h2>Sources and evidence anchors</h2><details id="source-web26-conor"><summary>Jefferies specialist sales / Conor O’Mara; Asia trip with Sherman (2026-09-26) · Five ideas and key themes from a week marketing around Asia with Sherman</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-26T14:00:00Z · Specialist-sales email read in authenticated Outlook web · <a href="https://outlook.cloud.microsoft/mail/id/AAQkADllY2NkMmU1LTc3YTEtNGRkMC1hMjBkLWU1NjIzOTY5OTZhMQAQALUQThwYi7tKoK5cVgKVwKM%3D">Original source</a></p><blockquote>Globally Lumentum is the best play on this</blockquote><blockquote>The big debate is whether its CPO or NPO.</blockquote><blockquote>Sherman sees HBM prices declining slightly next year</blockquote><blockquote>Some investors think AMD can do 5-7 m Venice CPUs. Sherman thinks this is too high hes at 3m.</blockquote></details><details id="source-web24-damnang"><summary>Damnang Research / Damnang and Aurelion Research (2026-09-24) · Ciena &amp; Fabrinet: The Road Ahead for Optics</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-24T22:35:00Z · Independent publication with reported IR conversations; full email text available, embedded charts not extracted · <a href="https://outlook.cloud.microsoft/mail/id/AAQkADllY2NkMmU1LTc3YTEtNGRkMC1hMjBkLWU1NjIzOTY5OTZhMQAQAMSpygkzEUJHpPAohvkb%2B8w%3D">Original source</a></p><blockquote>Bargaining power instead tends to arise at the supplier of a key component when that component is scarce.</blockquote><blockquote>we are not adding either company to the Aurelion Index at this time.</blockquote><blockquote>Making hard-to-make products well does not bring pricing power by itself</blockquote></details><details id="source-public:nvda-buyback"><summary>NVIDIA newsroom / NVIDIA (2026-09-28) · Share repurchase authorization increase</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28 · Primary company release; announcement, not executed repurchases · <a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-a-150-billion-share-repurchase-authorization-increase">Original source</a></p><blockquote>The company expects to execute the total remaining program through fiscal year 2028.</blockquote></details><details id="source-web28-barclays"><summary>Barclays TMT desk / Jeffrey Rand; relaying Tom O’Malley and Tim Long (2026-09-28) · NVDA buyback thoughts; MU earnings and memory; semis; JBL preview</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28T11:22:00Z · Specialist-sales email read in authenticated Outlook web · <a href="https://outlook.cloud.microsoft/mail/id/AAQkADllY2NkMmU1LTc3YTEtNGRkMC1hMjBkLWU1NjIzOTY5OTZhMQAQAAVVBC24pFpKv8fuO0SDGCw%3D">Original source</a></p><blockquote>it does little to answer the longer-term ROI question for generalists</blockquote><blockquote>Overall investor sentiment on the memory space has turned cautious.</blockquote><blockquote>I don’t think it really changes the narrative on the name/space for either bulls or bears.</blockquote><blockquote>LOs were 86% better to sell while HFs were 54% better to buy.</blockquote><blockquote>why we think AMD is best positioned in this market</blockquote></details><details id="source-x:2104527754523771387"><summary>Selected X post / firstadopter (2026-09-28) · Nvidia announces a software platform and monitoring tools for building safeguards for AI agents.

&quot;N</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28T11:04:51+00:00 · Original post / source-reported claim · <a href="https://x.com/firstadopter/status/2104527754523771387">Original source</a></p><blockquote>Nvidia announces a software platform and monitoring tools for building safeguards for AI agents.</blockquote></details><details id="source-web28-rothschild"><summary>Rothschild &amp; Co Redburn / Madeleine Falkiner; relaying Rowan Adley and house analysts (2026-09-28) · TOP IDEAS - Oracle, Nebius, CoreWeave (All Sells), Meta, Linde, Herc (All Buys), The Review</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28T13:01:00Z · Specialist-sales email read in authenticated Outlook web · <a href="https://outlook.cloud.microsoft/mail/inbox/id/AAQkADllY2NkMmU1LTc3YTEtNGRkMC1hMjBkLWU1NjIzOTY5OTZhMQAQAIfya9oGObhAr2b%2Ft%2FWQl9k%3D">Original source</a></p><blockquote>gave us the first real glimpse of a future where Meta truly is its own platform/ecosystem</blockquote><blockquote>we think site level delays are actually the pressure point.</blockquote><blockquote>Oracle, Nebius and CoreWeave</blockquote><blockquote>If Meta internalizes the storefront and commerce stack from H2, Shopify’s growth could slow materially.</blockquote></details><details id="source-web28-jpm-silver"><summary>J.P. Morgan TMT specialist sales / Scott Silver; relaying Marcus Diebel and Doug Anmuth (2026-09-28) · Silver Sunrise: Muse vs EU Classifieds; client positioning</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28T06:03:00Z · Specialist-sales email read in authenticated Outlook web · <a href="https://outlook.cloud.microsoft/mail/id/AAQkADllY2NkMmU1LTc3YTEtNGRkMC1hMjBkLWU1NjIzOTY5OTZhMQAQAOPgI7xdN2FBkq2vnFwDpGA%3D">Original source</a></p><blockquote>indicating limits to the agent orchestration/control plane under extreme concurrent load</blockquote><blockquote>few materially upweighting/re-grossing</blockquote></details><details id="source-4be34ee57271"><summary>Bernstein / Tyler Seidman (2026-09-24) · Bernstein Tech: META Connect thoughts (+ -), Gemini 4.0 is imminent (= +), AMZN positions for agentic adoption (+), QCOM extends AAPL agreement (=), Nscale readx to CRWV/IREN</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-24T13:12:11Z · Specialist sales · <a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058B9D43570000">Original source</a></p><blockquote>A bit underwhelming given recent Muse excitement (my view).</blockquote></details><details id="source-x:2104344675461054479"><summary>Selected X post / DanielTNiles (2026-09-27) · Last wk, Muse from $Meta (+12.9%) &amp; co-Pilot overhaul by $MSFT (+4.5%) drove AI infrastructure stren</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-27T22:57:22+00:00 · Original post / source-reported claim · <a href="https://x.com/DanielTNiles/status/2104344675461054479">Original source</a></p><blockquote>Microsoft which I posted about last Sunday is also a favored name</blockquote><blockquote>In the disruption fears category above, Google is the one that I am most bullish on.</blockquote></details><details id="source-public:nvda-safety"><summary>NVIDIA newsroom / NVIDIA (2026-09-28) · Open Agent Safety Platform</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28 · Primary company release; company-stated capabilities and ecosystem participation · <a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/open-agent-safety-platform">Original source</a></p><blockquote>Microsoft</blockquote><blockquote>Salesforce and NVIDIA have integrated OpenShell with Slack</blockquote><blockquote>Palo Alto Networks</blockquote></details><details id="source-x:2104402999997325484"><summary>Selected X post / FundaAI (2026-09-28) · Weekly|Consumer Agents Take Center Stage, Expert Network for Independent Researchers, Meta Muse, CPU</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28T02:49:07+00:00 · Original post / source-reported claim · <a href="https://x.com/FundaAI/status/2104402999997325484">Original source</a></p><blockquote>We expect tight supply and AI demand to support a higher, longer memory-price plateau</blockquote></details><details id="source-a0eca7b30e31"><summary>replytoanalyst@markit.esp.db.com / Brad Zelnick - Deutsche Bank (2026-09-24) · Oracle - Project Jupiter Update</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-24T16:26:36Z · Other selected email · <a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058B9D43B20000">Original source</a></p><blockquote>Project Jupiter remains on our planned schedule</blockquote></details><details id="source-72b5ce85ffae"><summary>Morgan Stanley / Thomas Wigg (2026-09-24) · MS TMT 9.24:  The AI trade transition from Enablers to Adopters; META reit Top Pick + GOOGL AMZN AAPL laterals; GOOGL Gemini 4 coming; SHOP + EXPE deets; ORCL BE delay; CSCO P OKTA bullish; SNPS iDay preview; IMAX init OW; TSM INTC IMAX DIS SPOT</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-24T13:51:30Z · Specialist sales · <a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058B9D43720000">Original source</a></p><blockquote>the key difference between Shop Pay (the button) vs Shopify Payments</blockquote><blockquote>Infrastructure &amp; Cybersecurity preferred such as MSFT, SNOW, CRWD, PANW, DDOG, NET, DT</blockquote></details><details id="source-x:2104494787927675318"><summary>Selected X post / ParadisLabs (2026-09-28) · Retail sentiment for semiconductor stocks also went up last week after a rough start to September.

</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-28T08:53:51+00:00 · Original post / source-reported claim · <a href="https://x.com/ParadisLabs/status/2104494787927675318">Original source</a></p><blockquote>Mag7&#x27;s were bought about 3 SD&#x27;s above normal</blockquote></details><details id="source-web26-semianalysis"><summary>SemiAnalysis / SemiAnalysis STEEL team / Dylan Patel; forwarded by Daniel Grozdea (2026-09-26) · Intel Panther Lake Teardown</summary><p>Source time 2026-09-26T13:38:00Z · Original technical publication forwarded by colleague; one underlying source · <a href="https://outlook.cloud.microsoft/mail/id/AAQkADllY2NkMmU1LTc3YTEtNGRkMC1hMjBkLWU1NjIzOTY5OTZhMQAQACVI%2BCTeFG1PrsyOP%2BQ5QZM%3D">Original source</a></p><blockquote>18A does not lead TSMC N3P, N2 or Samsung SF2 in peak density.</blockquote><blockquote>A sustained competitive lead depends on product performance, cost, yield, and the next implementation.</blockquote></details><footer>Selected source passages supporting 10 watchlist companies and 4 themes; retrieval matches are not reviewed opinions. No email attachments or survey charts were extracted. The broader specialist ledger remains dated 7–21 September.<br>Selected-account originals after text deduplication. Non-news accounts can include management/affiliates; authors are not necessarily independent. Vendor publication counts have separate coverage.<br>417 metadata screened; 141 bodies retrieved; 9 emails and 4 X posts cited. Source weighting is editorial; quantitative score weights are unchanged. The broader specialist ledger remains dated.</footer></main></body></html>